<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="scenario_3_equation_in_a_table_cell" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 3 — Equation in a table cell</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a table where one of the cells contains a Word equation object rather than</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>table</keyword>
        <keyword>Equation</keyword>
        <keyword>equation</keyword>
        <keyword>object</keyword>
        <keyword>Scenario</keyword>
        <keyword>inside</keyword>
        <indexterm>table</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Equation</indexterm>
        <indexterm>equation</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
     <section>
     <p>Consider a table where one of the cells contains a Word equation object rather than plain text. For example, a reference table listing formulas alongside their descriptions.</p>
       <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <title>Equation inside a table cell</title>
         <tgroup cols="2">
           <colspec colname="c1"/>
           <colspec colname="c2"/>
           <thead>
             <row>
               <entry>
                 <b>.docx Style / Input</b>
               </entry>
               <entry>
                 <b>DITA Output</b>
               </entry>
             </row>
           </thead>
           <tbody>
             <row>
               <entry>[Table] — cell 1: "Transfer Rate" / cell 2: <b>[Equation object: R = B/T]</b>
               </entry>
               <entry>
                <codeblock id="codeblock_mkv_mmr_kkc">
&lt;simpletable>
  &lt;strow>
    &lt;stentry>Transfer Rate&lt;/stentry>
    &lt;stentry>
      &lt;equation-inline>
        &lt;mathml>
          &lt;math xmlns="..MathML">
            &lt;mrow>
              &lt;mi>R&lt;/mi>
              &lt;mo>=&lt;/mo>
              &lt;mfrac>
                &lt;mi>B&lt;/mi>
                &lt;mi>T&lt;/mi>
              &lt;/mfrac>
            &lt;/mrow>
          &lt;/math>
        &lt;/mathml>
      &lt;/equation-inline>
    &lt;/stentry>
  &lt;/strow>
&lt;/simpletable></codeblock>
              </entry>
             </row>
           </tbody>
         </tgroup>
       </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> The converter processes the equation object within the table cell and converts it to an <codeph>&lt;equation-inline&gt;</codeph> element containing MathML, placed inside the <codeph>&lt;stentry&gt;</codeph> or <codeph>&lt;entry&gt;</codeph> of the DITA table. The equation is treated as inline content within the cell and does not break out of the table boundary.</p>
   </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
